# Security and cache headers for Static Assets (security §14, D12.8).
#
# The CSP here carries the directives a <meta> tag cannot express — frame-ancestors is ignored
# in meta, and base-uri / form-action belong with it — and upgrade-insecure-requests, which a
# meta could carry but which belongs to the response, like the others (review of 24/11/2026,
# U17). Everything about scripts, styles,
# images and fonts is emitted by Astro as a meta CSP with per-file SHA-256 hashes
# (astro.config.ts, experimental.csp). The two policies are enforced independently, so no
# directive may appear in both — a header "style-src 'self'" would intersect with the meta
# policy and block the inlined stylesheet.
#
# form-action is 'none': no form of this site is ever submitted by the browser itself. The two
# fields are answered by scripts, the dialogs close by `method="dialog"` (which navigates
# nowhere, so the directive does not concern it — tried in three engines on 14/11/2026). With
# 'self', Enter pressed before the search script had loaded sent the typed words to the server
# in the address; now the submission is stopped where it starts, and the fields have no name.
#
# HOW RULES COMBINE — read this before adding one. Every rule that matches a request applies, in
# file order, and a header set by two of them is JOINED with a comma, not replaced (Cloudflare
# docs, "Custom headers"). Measured on 12/11/2026 under `wrangler dev`, before this file was ever
# deployed: as first written, it served the fonts with
# "public, max-age=300, public, max-age=31536000, immutable" — two max-age values, which a cache
# is entitled to treat as stale — and the kill switch with "public, max-age=300, no-cache".
# A specific rule must first DETACH what "/*" set ("! Header-Name"), then set its own value.
# "/*" stays first; scripts/headers.test.ts holds both points.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# The preview host (D15.12) is where the app is built before launch: never indexed. An absolute
# URL scopes the rule to that hostname, so the apex is untouched.
https://beta.cestecritla.fr/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Content-addressed by the build: safe to freeze for a year.
/_astro/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
# NOT content-addressed: three fixed names, copied as they are (scripts/build-fonts.ts). Frozen
# for a year all the same, so their bytes never change under the same name — a gate holds them
# (scripts/check-build.test.ts): a new subset is a new name (review of 24/11/2026, U15).
/fonts/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Every file here carries in its name the fingerprint of what it holds (src/lib/search-data.ts,
# src/lib/words-data.ts, src/lib/fingerprint.ts): a file that changes gets a new name, never new
# bytes under an old one, so these can be frozen too — scripts/check-build.test.ts holds it. NOT
# the version of the book: the index and its titles carried it until 23/11/2026, the titles
# changed under it, every browser that had searched kept the old file, and « Demander » searched
# for ever (R73).
#
# Never indexed (D19.6): these are the files pages download, not pages. Since 18 November 2026
# the file of the game may hold OUR sentences about measures — written and checked by an AI,
# labelled as such on the card that shows them. Read alone by a search engine they would be an
# AI's sentences about a programme with no label next to them: so no engine is given them.
# (On the preview host this header leaves twice, « noindex, noindex » — the same word.)
/data/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# The share preview has a fixed name, /og/cestecritla-v1.png, drawn once by a local tool
# (scripts/og-image.ts) — not versioned by the build. Frozen for a year, so its bytes never
# change under that name: a gate holds them, and a new drawing is a new name (U15).
/og/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The only client-side kill switch (D12.8): one field, `silence_override`. Revalidated on every
# start, BEFORE effectiveDate(). Never immutable, never stale-while-revalidate: those would
# make the L49 freeze unreachable.
/flags.json
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8

# The server routes are `/api/gists` and `/api/chat`, answered on the exact addresses by the
# Worker of the sentences (wrangler.chat.jsonc), and on the preview `/api/bench`, by the Worker
# of the pages (wrangler.jsonc, `run_worker_first`). Those Workers set these headers themselves
# — this file is not applied to a Worker's own responses. Here they shape what the files answer
# under /api/ on the apex (a 404, a 405), and the two addresses if their Worker were withdrawn:
# never cacheable, never referrer-leaking (review of 24/11/2026, U16).
/api/*
  ! Cache-Control
  ! Referrer-Policy
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
